 ### Fixed
 
+- Two holds rule OD4 exposed (owner choice 2026-10-20 "Option 1: keep OD4", same batch folder, `OD4_HOLDS_REVIEW.md`, `MOVED_REFERENCES.md`; uncommitted at writing): the active-set cycle key carries each pass's static columns, so a closed valve pass under a junction's gas column is no longer refused as a repeat of the one under its water column (bundled seed 145, E7; main's gate `aJunctionCarriedAcrossAReplacementHasItsBufferSizedOnWhatItHolds` passes again); a junction's arriving-phase seed is the fluid-only PH split of stock and deliveries, not a TP flash at the mixed temperature, so liquid water reaching a cavitating pump suction stays liquid beside its flash steam (bundled seed 889, E9).
 - Walkway closed ends (owner report 2026-10-17, same batch folder, `MACHINES_HEATERS_THIRD_REVIEW.md`): a walkway's closed end now stops the player. Its end fence was 0.1 m thick and fell between the collision's 1/8-block sample points, so it had no hitbox; closed ends now use the side rails' 0.2 m band, and a gate checks that every closed end of every heater deck fills collision voxels. The constructor screen's hints for compressor bore and throws and for VC heater diameter and height now give the second pass's ranges, and the cabin's hint names its radiant header boxes as seen from the constructor (in at the left, out at the right; the nozzles did not move).
 - Constructor ghost under shader packs (owner report 2026-10-17, same batch folder, `GHOST_PIPE_SPACING_REVIEW.md`): the translucent preview vanished under Iris (Complementary Reimagined); it was drawn with the chunk type `RenderType.translucent()` from a level-stage event, which Iris's terrain programs do not take. It is now translucent entity geometry on the block atlas (`RenderType.entityTranslucentCull`), as Catnip draws its outlines, and shows in vanilla, under Sodium and under Iris.
 - Pipe spacing (owner rule 2026-10-17, "piping connection should have 1 block spacing between them to prevent misconnection", same batch folder, `GHOST_PIPE_SPACING_REVIEW.md`): pipes in blocks that share a face join, and 110 nozzle pairs had touching pipe blocks (every vertical heater, cabins with short convection sections, small exchangers and kettles, the smallest ejectors, column draws and pumparounds on neighbouring trays). `EquipmentShape.Nozzle.crowds` (pipe blocks touching by a face, an edge or a corner) is now one rule: a drum's side connections that crowd clash, a column's side nozzles take the nearest row that crowds none, and the units' layouts keep one free block: heater convection sections at least tall enough for their inlet two rows over their outlet and the vertical heater's radiant inlet two rows under it, exchanger and kettle shell nozzles two rows behind the channel's (saddles off the pipe blocks under the shell, `saddleAt`), the small ejector's motive stub two rows over its suction. Gate: every unit size, the test columns and drums.
